<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ruth Shady</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Ruth Shady Solís</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ruth Shady Solís is a Peruvian archaeologist who has led excavations at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caral">Caral</a> in the Supe valley since 1994. Her radiocarbon dates showed that Caral was a large planned centre by about 2600 BCE, making the Caral-Supe civilisation one of the oldest in the world. She led the effort that made Caral a World Heritage Site in 2009.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ruth-shady.jpg" alt="Ruth Shady" width="320" height="375" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ruth Madelen Luna Cruz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ruth_Shady_en_Caral_2014_(cropped).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
